Column Validation Rules

Dataset: Superstore Sales

This document describes validation rules for each column in the cleaned Superstore dataset.

Column| Data Type| Validation Rule
Order Date| Date| Must contain valid dates
Region| Text| Must contain valid region names
State| Text| Must not be empty
Category| Text| Must contain valid categories
Sub-Category| Text| Must not be empty
Segment| Text| Must contain valid customer segments
Sales| Decimal| Must contain numeric values
Profit| Decimal| Must contain numeric values
Quantity| Integer| Must contain whole numbers

General Validation Checks

1. Check for missing values.
2. Identify duplicate records.
3. Verify column data types.
4. Validate date formats.
5. Check numerical columns for invalid values.
6. Verify categorical column values.

Expected Dataset Structure

- Total Records: 9,994
- Total Columns: 9
- Missing Values: 0
- Invalid Dates: 0

Conclusion

Column validation rules help maintain data accuracy, consistency, and reliability. These checks support the preparation of a clean dataset for further analysis.
